NXR-112|Native C# host tool targets|Tooling|Every project C# host tool with Native AOT support shall provide a native publish target and execute natively by default throughout CMake, CTest and firmware auditing.|Use native executables without requiring a .NET runtime at execution time while preserving C# source and XDoc.|Publish audit, tracker and configurator for build-host OS/CPU, never firmware ISA; native_tools builds all; tests and ELF audits invoke executables directly; XML docs emitted beside binaries; reflection JSON disabled with generated metadata; AOT/linker warnings fail; unsupported hosts require explicit managed compatibility selection; Linux native self-tests, tracker import/generation and firmware audit pass.|Native publish logs, executable format inspection, CTest command inspection, all CLI self-tests and RV32 audit/static-contract build using host-native tools.|NXR-076,NXR-085,NXR-087,NXR-101|RTOS_NATIVE_TOOLS=ON default; OFF explicitly enables managed compatibility; host-specific RID.|Native host tools may use host heap; firmware pools/stacks and noheap audits unchanged; separate host build output directories.|cmake/host-tools.cmake,cmake/requirements.cmake,cmake/configure-tool.cmake,tools/Rtos.Tools/Rtos.Tools.csproj,tools/NexRT.Requirements/NativeJson.cs,tools/NexRT.Configure/NativeJson.cs,docs/tooling.rst|Three C# projects have Native AOT targets and generated JSON metadata; host-specific builds require SDK/compiler prerequisites and only tested hosts can claim execution evidence.|cmake/host-tools.cmake,tools/NexRT.Requirements/NativeJson.cs,tools/NexRT.Configure/NativeJson.cs||PartialSourceUnverified
